// EXPECT: PASS
// The object's *own* declared path (before the ':') resolves its first
// component the same way an implicit (dot-less) supertype name does:
// ascend the object tree as many levels as it takes, not just one - and,
// same rule either way, no ascent at all once any name has matched.
// "Deep" is three levels up the tree from z (at TOP). Was previously
// (wrongly) rejected: start_object()'s own descent loop allowed only one
// ascend-and-retry for the whole path (adlstore.h's "may_ascend" was used
// once, not reset per name), failing with "The name `Deep` on the way to
// the parent was not found" after ascending only as far as y. Fixed
// 2026-09-26.
TOP {
	Deep: {
		Item:;
	}
	x: {
		y: {
			z: {
				Deep.Item.NewChild: {}
			}
		}
	}
}
